# oracle: pair_style pace/extrapolation with a linear active set: a self-made single-element B-basis (ranks 1-5, ChebExpCos, FinnisSinclairShiftedScaled, distance inner cutoff with core repulsion; scripts/oracle/pace-extrapolation-fixtures.py) on a displaced fcc Cu cell, the grade and the core-repulsion factor from fix pair every 5 steps, 300 K NVE
# Native reference: LAMMPS b332f28 built with PKG_ML-PACE (the installed binary has no ML-PACE)
# Measured with native LAMMPS: max relative error engine vs native thermo 6.6e-13, atoms 1.8e-15.
# oracle-inputs: pace_al_cu.yaml pace_al_cu.asi
# oracle-compare: thermo=all atoms=all
units           metal
atom_style      atomic
lattice         fcc 3.6
region          box block 0 3 0 3 0 3
create_box      1 box
create_atoms    1 box
mass            1 63.546
displace_atoms  all random 0.1 0.1 0.1 12345 units box
pair_style      pace/extrapolation
pair_coeff      * * pace_al_cu.yaml pace_al_cu.asi Cu
fix             grade all pair 5 pace/extrapolation gamma 1 corerep 1
compute         gmax all reduce max f_grade[1] f_grade[2]
compute         gsum all reduce sum f_grade[1]
velocity        all create 300 4928 loop geom
fix             1 all nve
thermo_style    custom step pe ke etotal press pxy c_gmax[1] c_gmax[2] c_gsum
thermo_modify   format float %.15g
thermo          5
run             20
